1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:09,900
If you work in the trades, you know this search. You need one used part, or one machine for a job, so you open every site and app you can think of.

2
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:19,330
You scroll past cars, couches and listings that have nothing to do with your work. It takes hours. A lot of the time, you find nothing.

3
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:27,250
So you buy new and wait for it to come in. And the job waits with it.

4
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:37,100
The whole time, the part you needed might be sitting in someone's yard across town.

5
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:53,280
That is why we built YardSwaps. One place for the trades and small businesses to find used equipment and parts close by, at a competitive price, from people who already have them sitting there.

6
00:00:53,876 --> 00:01:03,496
Search by name or part number and set how far you will drive. Message the seller or send an offer, then meet up. You see it and run it before you pay.

7
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:34,570
It works the other way too. Most shops and yards have equipment or parts sitting around that someone else needs. Take a photo and the app fills in the listing for you. Listing is free, and there is no selling fee.

8
00:01:35,172 --> 00:01:42,782
That spare pump, the old trailer, the donor machine out back. A free listing can turn them into extra cash flow for your business.

9
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:56,970
We are a small team in El Paso, Texas. If you need something, search YardSwaps before you buy new. If it is sitting in your yard, list it free.

